//--------------------//

rpi-image-gen is an additional layer on top of the Debian build system. Here's what it adds:

1. Raspberry Pi-specific image creation

- Takes Debian's binary packages and assembles them into bootable Raspberry Pi images
- Handles RPi-specific partitioning, boot firmware, and device tree configurations
- The Debian build system just creates .deb packages - it doesn't create SD card images

2. Declarative configuration

- Uses YAML-based profiles, image layouts, and configuration files
- You define WHAT you want (packages, users, settings) rather than HOW to build it
- Much simpler than writing shell scripts to call debootstrap manually

3. Modular composition

- Profiles are collections of packages and operations that can be combined
- Mix and match components (base system + WiFi + your app + security hardening)
- Reusable building blocks for different image variants

4. Enterprise/Industrial features

- Generates Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) for compliance
- Creates CVE (security vulnerability) reports
- Integrates with rpi-sb-provisioner for secure boot and encrypted filesystems

5. Reproducible builds

- Same config = same image every time
- Perfect for CI/CD pipelines
- Version control your image definitions

