Layers in rpi-image-gen are NOT like Yocto layers. They're much simpler:A layer is a single YAML file that describes packages to install and operations to perform on the root filesystem LinuxGizmosGitHub. Think of it more like a "recipe" or "building block."

Key concepts:

1. Layer = Single YAML file with metadata (packages + operations)
2. Profile = A collection of layers grouped together
3. Config = INI-style file that selects which profile and disk layout to use

//--------------------//
//--------------------//
//--------------------//

Config File (.ini format)
    ↓ references
Profile (collection of layers)
    ↓ includes
Multiple Layer Files (YAML)
    ↓ each defines
Packages + Operations

